# acl-broker - the Mini Smart Home broker's access list (Module 21).
# Mosquitto reads this file from top to bottom. A line starting with # is a note (# must be the first character of the line).
# An account not mentioned here may not write or read anything.
# Every time this file changes, RESTART the broker (not reload). Module 26, the broker in Docker Compose: docker compose restart
# mosquitto (from the project root for the central broker, from the edge folder on the Pi for the gateway broker).

# 1) Each device may only "talk" on its own topics. A pattern line applies to ALL accounts;
#    %u is replaced by the username proven with a password, that is, that device's device_id.
pattern write msh/%u/telemetry
pattern write msh/%u/status
pattern write msh/%u/vitals
pattern write msh/%u/ack
pattern read msh/%u/cmd

# 2) One exception in the data contract (rule 6): Node 1 publishes Node 2's telemetry and status.
#    Replace a4cf12e5b7c0 with your Node 1's device_id and 246f28b1c7d4 with your Node 2's device_id.
user a4cf12e5b7c0
topic write msh/246f28b1c7d4/telemetry
topic write msh/246f28b1c7d4/status

# 2b) Laptop path (Module 25): the "mock Garden" f00d000000b2 is published by the first fake device f00d00000001 (simulator in
#     tools/), exactly like item 2. Only for readers WITHOUT a real Node 2: delete "# " (the hash and its space) in front of
#     the three lines below, save, then RESTART the broker. Readers with Kit A + B don't need this block.
# user f00d00000001
# topic write msh/f00d000000b2/telemetry
# topic write msh/f00d000000b2/status

# 3) Backend: reads all device messages, sends commands (set and config) to cmd.
user backend
topic read msh/#
topic write msh/+/cmd

# 4) Node-RED on the Pi gateway: the dashboard reads, the Fan switch sends cmd.
user nodered
topic read msh/#
topic write msh/+/cmd

# 5) The contract checker (tools/contract-checker.js): read only.
user checker
topic read msh/#

# 6) Monitor (MQTTX, mosquitto_sub): looks only, including the broker statistics in $SYS.
user monitor
topic read msh/#
topic read $SYS/#

# 7) The Pi gateway bridge (Module 26): applies on the CENTRAL broker (compose.cloud.yml), where the bridge logs in with this account.
#    The bridge forwards the messages of all devices to the center and picks up the commands for them. The per-device checks
#    (items 1 and 2) are already done by the gateway broker on the Pi, which uses the same file but has no pi-bridge account.
user pi-bridge
topic write msh/+/telemetry
topic write msh/+/status
topic write msh/+/vitals
topic write msh/+/ack
topic read msh/+/cmd
